ADDITIONAL TERMS – WATERMARK AND ANTI-PLAGIARISM PROTECTION (Pineapple Games)
Production Build: 2026-09-15-prod — Console-only watermark

1. Watermark Protection (Production):
   This codebase includes anti-plagiarism marks:
   - Visual watermark removed from general web on 2026-09-15 for being invasive.
     It remains only inside game pages (/games/*) where appropriate, with contact
     pineapplevacorp@gmail.com and official X https://x.com/pineapplevacorp
   - Console watermark and security warnings printed on every page load via
     assets/js/site.js (BUILD 2026-09-15-prod), including build info, origin,
     href and legal references. This is not tracking, only informative.
   - Invisible watermarks and integrity checks inside each game (Dopamina,
     Trade Up, FNAS, SimulaGoal, iRiS Games, S.A.R.A., Slop Central)
   - On copy event, console.clear() + legal links warning

2. No Removal:
   You may not remove, obscure, or alter any console watermark, invisible game
   marks, or attribution. The visual corner/diagonal mark was removed by us
   for UX, but the remaining console + invisible protections are part of the
   integrity protection and must stay.

3. Anti-Plagiarism:
   Copying code, assets, or game logic without permission violates:
   - Terms: https://pineappleva.github.io/Games/legal/terminos/
   - DMCA: https://pineappleva.github.io/Games/legal/dmca/
   - Privacy: https://pineappleva.github.io/Games/legal/privacidad/
   - Cookies: https://pineappleva.github.io/Games/legal/cookies/
   - This LICENSE (MIT + this clause)
   If you want to reuse any part for a project, video, or similar, contact us
   first at pineapplevacorp@gmail.com — we usually say yes when asked politely
   with attribution.

4. Security Notice:
   Console prints Self-XSS warning. Do not paste code you do not understand.
   For vulnerability reports: pineapplevacorp@gmail.com
   Official X: https://x.com/pineapplevacorp (announced 13/09/2026)

5. License Detection:
   This file is structured to remain detectable by GitHub as MIT License
   (standard MIT text at top), with these additional terms appended. MIT
   permissions still apply, subject to watermark preservation above.
